{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "BioAPI",
    "description": "# 🧬 Welcome to BioAPI\n\nBioAPI unifies biomedical datasets behind a consistent, queryable interface.\nUse familiar operators to filter, paginate with cursors, and receive predictable\nJSON responses across all endpoints.\n\n> [!tip]\n> New to the API? Read through this short guide below. **Read time: 5-10 minutes**\n\n<!-- > [!TIP]\n> New to the API? Start with [Authentication](#authentication), then explore the [Database](#tag/Database) endpoints. -->\n\n---\n\n\n# 🔑 Authentication\n\nInclude your API key in the `X-API-Key` header with every request:\n```bash\ncurl https://api.bioapi.dev/v1/endpoint \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: your_api_key_here\"\n```\n\n**Example with fetch:**\n```javascript\nfetch('https://api.bioapi.dev/v1/users', {\n  headers: {\n    'X-API-Key': 'your_api_key_here'\n  }\n})\n```\n<!-- \n> You can view or create your API key in the [API Keys section](https://app.example.com/dashboard/api-keys) of your dashboard. Keep it secure and never commit it to version control. -->\n\n> [!note]\n> You can view or create your API key in the [dashboard](https://bioapi.dev/dashboard/keys). Keep it secure and never commit it to version control.\n\n---\n\n#  🚀 Quick Start\n\n### Base URL\n```\nhttps://api.bioapi.dev/v1\n```\n\n### Basic Request\n```bash\ncurl \"https://api.bioapi.dev/database/press-releases/fda/rss?limit=5\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: your-api-key\"\n```\n\n### Python Example\n```python\nimport requests\n\nheaders = {\"X-API-Key\": \"your-api-key\"}\nparams = {\"limit\": 10, \"pub_date.gte\": \"2024-01-01\"}\n\nresponse = requests.get(\n    \"https://api.bioapi.dev/database/press-releases/fda/rss\",\n    headers=headers,\n    params=params\n)\n\nfor item in response.json()[\"data\"]:\n    print(item[\"title\"])\n```\n\n### JavaScript Example\n```javascript\nconst response = await fetch(\n  'https://api.bioapi.dev/database/press-releases/fda/rss?limit=10',\n  { headers: { 'X-API-Key': 'your-api-key' } }\n);\n\nconst { data, total, next_token } = await response.json();\nconsole.log(`Found ${total} results`);\n```\n\n---\n\n# 🔍 Filtering & Querying\n\n### Basic Filters\nUse equality for exact matches:\n```http\n?status=active&country=US\n```\n\n### Operators\nAppend operators for advanced filtering:\n\n#### String Operators\n\n| Operator | Description | Example |\n|----------|-------------|---------|\n| `field` | Exact match | `?name=John`|\n| `field.regex` | Regular expression | `?name.regex=^J.*` |\n| `field.like` | Pattern match <br/>(case-sensitive) | `?name.like=%John%` |\n| `field.ilike` | Pattern match <br/>(case-insensitive) | `?name.ilike=%john%` |\n\n#### Numeric & Date Operators\n\n| Operator | Description | Example |\n|----------|-------------|---------|\n| `field` | Exact match | `?age=18` |\n| `field.gt` | Greater than | `?age.gt=18` |\n| `field.gte` | Greater than or equal | `?age.gte=18` |\n| `field.lt` | Less than | `?age.lt=65` |\n| `field.lte` | Less than or equal |`?age.lte=65` |\n\n#### Nullable Operators\nApplies to all parameters marked *nullable* regardless of type:\n| Operator | Description | Example |\n|----------|-------------|---------|\n| `field.isnull` | Field is null | `?email.isnull=true` |\n\n\n\n### Date Range Example\n```\n# Inclusive start, exclusive end pattern\n?pub_date.gte=2024-01-01&pub_date.lt=2024-02-01\n```\n> [!NOTE]\n> Use ISO 8601 format for dates: `2024-01-01` or `2024-01-01T12:00:00Z`\n\n### Multiple Values\nPass multiple values as CSV (comma-separated) or repeated parameters:\n```bash\n# CSV format\n?classification=ClassI,ClassII\n\n# Repeated format\n?classification=ClassI&classification=ClassII\n```\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Only base equality filters (`field=value`) accept multiple values. Operators like `field.gt=value` take a single value.\n---\n\n# 📑 Pagination\n\n- `limit` controls page size (default `100`, max `1000`).\n- When more results exist, a `next_token` is returned.\n- Pass `next_token` back with the same query to fetch the next page.\n\n```bash\n# First page\ncurl \"https://bioapi.dev/database/endpoint?limit=100\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: your-api-key\"\n\n# Next page (use token from previous response)\ncurl \"https://bioapi.dev/database/endpoint?limit=100&next_token=abc123\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: your-api-key\"\n```\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Pagination Tokens are query-specific. If you change filters, start fresh without `next_token`.\n\n---\n\n# 📋 Response Format\n\nAll endpoints return consistent JSON:\n```json\n{\n  \"data\": [{ /* records */ }],\n  \"limit\": 100,\n  \"total\": 1234,\n  \"next_token\": \"abc123...\"\n}\n```\n<!-- Fields:\n- `data`: array of results matching your query\n- `limit`: page size used for this request\n- `total`: total number of matching records\n- `next_token`: token for fetching the next page (not included if no more results) -->\n\n| Field | Description |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `data` | Array of results matching your query |\n| `limit` | Page size used for this request |\n| `total` | Total number of matching records |\n| `next_token` | Token for fetching the next page <br/> (not included if no more results) |\n\n---\n# 🌐 Database Endpoints \n**Base path:** `/database`\n\nBioAPI aggregates data from multiple biomedical sources:\n\n- **FDA** — Press releases, MedWatch, Drugs@FDA, enforcement actions\n- **ClinicalTrials.gov** — Study registry data\n- **DailyMed** — SPL labeling information\n- **Orange Book / Purple Book** — Reference datasets\n- **Industry news** — Drugs.com, PharmaLive feeds\n\nEndpoints are grouped by coverage area below.\n\n> [!success]\n> Endpoints are updated on their own cadences and normalized into consistent models for downstream use.\n\n---\n\n# 💬 Questions or Issues?\n\nContact us at [support@bioapi.dev](mailto:support@bioapi.dev).\n\n\n<!-- ## 🗂️ Data Sources\n\nOur API covers regulatory, labeling, study registry, reference books, and\nindustry news sources. See the [Database](#tag/Database) tag for the full list,\nupdate cadences, and per-endpoint fields.\n\n## 🔗 Explore the API\n\n> [!tip]\n> Ready to dive in? Browse the [**Database**](#tag/Database) endpoints to see models, filters, and examples. -->\n",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "x-jentic-source-url": "https://bioapi.dev/openapi.json"
  },
