    {
      "name": "Database",
      "description": "🗄️ **Database Endpoints**\n\nAccess normalized biomedical datasets with a single, consistent interface. All\nendpoints share the same query operators, pagination model, and response shape.\n\n> [!tip]\n> Every endpoint supports filtering, list-style parameters, and cursor pagination with `next_token`.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Base path: `/database`\n- Auth header: `X-API-Key: <your-key>`\n- Limit: default `100`, max `1000`\n- Pagination: `next_token` is returned when more results are available\n\n## Query Operators\n\nUse simple equality for most fields, or add an operator suffix using\n`field.operator`. Equals parameters accept comma-separated values or repeated\nkeys (`field=val1,val2&field=val3`). Operations (`field.operator`) do not accept multiple values.\n\n- String: `field` (equals), `field.like`, `field.ilike`, `field.regex`, `field.isnull`\n- Integer/Datetime: `field` (equals), `field.gt`, `field.gte`, `field.lt`, `field.lte`, `field.isnull`\n\nExamples:\n\n```http\n# Equality (string)\n?applicant=Pfizer\n\n# Case-insensitive substring\n?title.ilike=vaccin\n\n# Datetime range (inclusive start, exclusive end pattern)\n?pub_date.gte=2024-01-01&pub_date.lt=2024-02-01\n\n# Multiple values (Comma seperated or repeated)\n?ticker=AAPL,MSFT  \n?ticker=AAPL&ticker=MSFT\n```\n\n> [!note]\n> Unknown fields or invalid operators return clear 400 errors. A `next_token` is only valid for the exact query that produced it.\n\n## Response Envelope\n\n```json\n{\n  \"data\": [ { /* records */ } ],\n  \"limit\": 100,\n  \"total\": 123,\n  \"next_token\": \"eyJjdXJzb3IiOi...\" // nullable\n}\n```\n\n## Typical Sources\n\n- FDA (press releases, MedWatch, Drugs@FDA, enforcement)\n- ClinicalTrials.gov (study registry)\n- DailyMed (SPL labeling)\n- Orange Book / Purple Book (reference datasets)\n- Industry news feeds (Drugs.com, PharmaLive)\n\n> [!success]\n> Endpoints are updated on their own cadences and normalized into consistent models for downstream use.\n\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "Test",
      "description": "🧪 **Test Endpoints** - Development and testing utilities for API validation and debugging.\n\n> [!warning]\n> These endpoints are primarily for development, monitoring, and integration testing.\n\n**Available Tests:**\n- API Health Checks - Verify service availability\n- Authentication Testing - Validate API keys  \n- Response Validation - Test data formats and structures\n- Performance Testing - Measure response times\n\n> [!important]\n> Use these endpoints to ensure your integration is working correctly before going to production.\n"
    }
